  "reason": "The records collectively provide a plausible route to the later result. R6, R10, R14, and R16 establish milling-time control of refinement, solid-solution formation, hardness, and contamination in mechanically alloyed HEAs, while R20 addresses phase retention or decomposition during sintering. R8 supplies especially close compositional-system evidence that severe deformation refines AlCoCrFeNi-type alloys, and R2/R13 connect dislocation density to hardness in a Co-Cr-Fe-Ni-based alloy. Other records establish grain-refinement and solid-solution strengthening and composition-dependent phase stability. Although no record states the exact equimolar CoCrFeNiTi, 1–6 hour HEBM plus 900–1000 °C SPS recipe or the precise 83% FCC/17% BCC result, an expert could plausibly combine the documented mechanical-alloying, rapid-sintering, grain-refinement, dislocation, and phase-stability principles to propose it."
